<ent/plugins/qa/subscription-lifecycle-test/kanban# kanban-md --help
kanban-md is a CLI tool for managing Kanban boards using plain Markdown files.
Tasks are stored as individual files with YAML frontmatter, making them
easy to read, edit, and version-control. Designed for AI agents and humans alike.

Usage:
  kanban-md [command]

Available Commands:
  agent-name  Generate a unique agent name for claims
  archive     Archive a task (soft-delete)
  board       Show board summary
  completion  Generate shell completion script
  config      View or modify board configuration
  context     Generate a board context summary
  create      Create a new task
  delete      Delete a task
  edit        Edit a task
  handoff     Hand off a task (move to review with notes)
  help        Help about any command
  init        Initialize a new kanban board
  list        List tasks
  log         Show activity log
  metrics     Show flow metrics
  move        Move a task to a different status
  pick        Pick the next available task
  show        Show task details
  skill       Manage agent skills
  tui         Open the interactive board UI

Flags:
      --compact      compact one-line-per-record output
      --dir string   path to kanban directory
  -h, --help         help for kanban-md
      --json         output as JSON
      --no-color     disable color output
      --oneline      alias for --compact
      --table        output as table
  -v, --version      version for kanban-md

Use "kanban-md [command] --help" for more information about a command.
<ent/plugins/qa/subscription-lifecycle-test/kanban# kanban-md list --help
Lists tasks with optional filtering, sorting, and output format control.

Usage:
  kanban-md list [flags]

Aliases:
  list, ls

Flags:
      --archived            show only archived tasks
      --assignee string     filter by assignee
      --blocked             show only blocked tasks
      --claimed-by string   filter by claimant
      --class string        filter by class of service
      --group-by string     group results by field (assignee, tag, class, priority, status)
  -h, --help                help for list
  -n, --limit int           limit number of results
      --not-blocked         show only non-blocked tasks
      --parent int          filter by parent task ID
      --priority strings    filter by priority (comma-separated)
  -r, --reverse             reverse sort order
  -s, --search string       search tasks by title, body, or tags (case-insensitive)
      --sort string         sort field (id, status, priority, created, updated, due) (default "id")
      --status strings      filter by status (comma-separated)
      --tag string          filter by tag
      --unblocked           show only tasks with all dependencies satisfied (missing dependency IDs are treated as satisfied)
      --unclaimed           show only unclaimed or expired-claim tasks

Global Flags:
      --compact      compact one-line-per-record output
      --dir string   path to kanban directory
      --json         output as JSON
      --no-color     disable color output
      --oneline      alias for --compact
      --table        output as table
